title: "claude-memory-tidy"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/claude-memory-tidy"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/claude-memory-tidy"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A deterministic toolkit for keeping an always-loaded agent memory index healthy. Claude
  Code loads MEMORY.md into every session and the harness truncates it past a fixed size
  with no error and no warning, so the index silently gets shorter and the agent quietly
  stops knowing things it remembers, while the notes on disk become orphaned: present but
  unreachable, which at recall time is the same as deleted. Three tiers - a hot dispatcher
  index, warm hubs, a cold archive - with mechanical work done by scripts and only the
  judgement call handed to a model, gated so a quiet day costs about zero tokens. Nothing
  is ever deleted; folding moves bytes verbatim and refuses to write if reachability would
  be lost.
keywords:
  - claude-code
  - agent-memory
